I read only the three permitted files. I can provide the census and structural ordering, but I can’t supply guest settings that reproduce host termination. No files were changed and no probe was run.

For the census, the producers matter first. In `do_mte_transfer()`, `mode` and `bytemask` come from stored 32-bit register values. The source and destination selectors are extracted three-bit fields. The depth producer yields **8, 16, 32, or 64 bits**: the header names only three depth encodings, but the extraction admits a fourth. Restricting the domain to the named constants would therefore be incorrect. See the [producer expressions](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1435) and [field definitions](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/crmfbreg.h:254).

